^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-13 00:00] observe — current runtime precipitates are concrete stage artifacts in src/runtime/pipeline/stages.ts, but docs/spec surfaces still mix older stage stories and looser chemistry language.
 >>[2026-03-13 00:01] decide — treat precipitate alignment as a semantics-rigor task first: define material roles before changing implementation names or checks.
 >>[2026-03-13 00:02] taste — the chemistry should stay operational: substrate is medium, precipitate is stable stage output, telemetry is assay, resonance is derived pattern.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:25] revise — commits retargeted to packages/spw-runtime/src/pipeline (src/runtime/pipeline is now a re-export shim) and made concrete; no runtime test references runSpwStepped or collectPrecipitates, so ~[3] is a real gap. Questions precipitate_boundary and telemetry_relation resolved by code: Precipitate in stages.ts is per-stage only (PipelineProjection is a keyed map of them) and RuntimeTelemetry is collected once per run by collectTelemetry, not per stage.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:25] observe — invariant stage_continuity (exactly one precipitate per stage) disagrees with the parse-failure branch in runSpwStepped, which returns after the parse precipitate; five malformed inputs I tried (}}}, unterminated string, mismatched brace, empty) all still parsed successfully and yielded four precipitates, so the branch is reachable only through errors I could not trigger. Opened failure_continuity and telemetry_locality.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:31] revise — convention: resolved questions and landed commits are kept in ^["done"] (resolved(label) and shipped) rather than deleted; ^["commits"] keeps a pointer comment.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:00] observe — six malformed inputs through runSpwStepped (}}} unterminated string unclosed bracket empty parens and a sigil mix) all returned success true with 4 precipitates, and normalize.test.ts covers success paths only; opened ?[failure_branch_test]; routed from lukewarm-backlog.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:27] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 2 landed, 3 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:04] revise — A runtime survey (runtime-maintenance) corrects one line here: runSpwStepped and collectPrecipitates are tested, in src/seed/__tests__/normalize.test.ts line 330, reached through the src/runtime shim and run by the seed suite; runtime-maintenance legacy_tests_home moves that test into the runtime package. split_stages is routed here.
 >>[2026-10-19 16:40] revise — Owner welcomes cognitive-surface redesign and IR/memory insight. Ground the proposed IR journey in existing Precipitate fields, distinguish ParseOutput from AST, and keep missing stage mappings explicit.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:24] observe — The order test that test_precipitate_order would add half exists: all four stages on success in src/seed/__tests__/normalize.test.ts (since df7c6056) lists desugar, parse, normalize, interpret literally, but inside if (result.success), so a failed run passes it. At 850077ab the malformed inputs }}}, an unterminated string, { [ } and the empty string all still return parse success true with 0 errors and 4 precipitates, so the parse-failure branch of failure_continuity stays unreached.
 >>[2026-11-09 18:12] note — wonder_trial_threshold_ladders is homed here: the runtime four-rung liminality, the seven surface waypoints and the three retention tiers sit beside six ladders hosts keep, and the liminality bridge declares the only crossing. docs/theory/spw/threshold-distance.spw lists all nine.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] note — Reheated from dormant to planning on the owner's direction of 2026-11-13: physical agility in small steps, each one a quantity that is counted and not only named. This plan's gates (operational truth, metaphor discipline) make it the home for a ledger of physical words; operational-topography holds the first new count, body outbound, and this plan does not repeat its commits.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Where field code lives: packages/spw-seed/src/math/field.ts, in the seed and not the runtime. Its ten tests pass (vitest.seed.config.ts). They hold: decay halves at one half-life; transfer keeps the sum; one symmetric diffuse step on two sites keeps the sum; capacityStep at rate 0.5 ends between 8 and 10 of 10; affinityAllocate never fills a site past its capacity and a carrier's bound and free amounts add to what it had.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — What the tests do not hold. flux(permeability, upstream, downstream) has no test and no caller in packages. A directed diffuse step loses the sum (a 1, b 0, one edge, kappa 0.25 gives a 0.75, b 0, sum 0.75), as its doc comment allows. A symmetric step with kappa times dt times weight above 1 goes negative (kappa 1.5 gives a -0.5, b 1.5). capacityStep at capacity 10 and rate 2.5 from 1 reads 3.25, 8.73, 11.5, 7.19, 12.24, so the invariant in docs/theory/spw/field-dynamics.spw, stays in 0 to K for r and x above 0, is false as written; it holds when rate times dt is at most 1.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Ledger of physical words today. Decay, capacity and conservation are computed and tested on numbers a caller supplies; no .spw surface and no runtime state supplies those numbers. Flux and permeability are computed and untested. Membrane is named in field-dynamics as a boundary law and has no code in field.ts. Charge in packages/spw-runtime/src/session/charge.ts is a packet with one of six lifecycle states and a provenance; portabilityHint scores it 0 to 1 and says of itself that it is not a physical force. Heat is one comment in state/memory-policy.ts. None of the seven is measured from a parsed surface.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] observe — Membrane already has two meanings. field-dynamics.spw: a boundary law, what may cross. packages/spw-runtime/src/session/composition-eval.ts: the host file an expression is evaluated in. em-fixity-association gives a third as a profile, the angle pair. Opened membrane_word before any commit adds a fourth.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] note — Breaks, where the likeness to physics stops. Charge here has no sign and no amount: two packets do not sum and none cancels. Conservation holds for transfer and undirected diffuse only; decay, inject and directed diffuse change the sum by design. Capacity is a ceiling the step can pass. Flux has a sign but nothing in the repo gives it a gradient, since no container carries an amplitude. The five valences are qualities and do not add.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:55] revise — Five planned commits added ahead of align_note_and_spec, one change each with its proof: test_flux_sign, test_capacity_bound, test_diffuse_bounds, correct_field_invariants, physical_word_ledger. Card next and next_commit now name test_flux_sign; touches gains math/field.ts. Opened capacity_bound, membrane_word and ledger_home.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[telemetry_locality]: "The invariant telemetry_locality says assays are local to the acting stage, but collectTelemetry runs once after the last stage; do we amend the invariant to say run-level, or add a per-stage assay slice to Precipitate?"
 ?[failure_continuity]: "stage_continuity says each stage MUST produce exactly one precipitate, but the parse-failure branch in runSpwStepped returns before normalize and interpret; do we restate the invariant as at-most-one, or make the failure branch yield empty precipitates?"
 ?[normalize_role]: "Is normalize best described as clarification, crystallization, or simply canonical reduction in the chemistry model?"
 ?[failure_branch_test]: "Which input reaches the parse-failure return in runSpwStepped (six malformed inputs I ran all returned success true), and does that branch get a test before failure_continuity is settled? Tracked at ~\"../lukewarm-backlog/wip.spw\" ?[precipitate_failure_untested]."
 ?[capacity_bound]: "capacityStep passes its capacity when rate times dt is above 1 (11.5 and 12.24 of 10 at rate 2.5); does the step clamp to the capacity, or does the invariant say rate times dt at most 1 and leave the overshoot as the logistic map it is?"
 ?[membrane_word]: "Membrane means a boundary law in field-dynamics, the host file of an evaluation in composition-eval, and the angle pair in em-fixity-association; which one keeps the word, and what are the other two called?"
 ?[ledger_home]: "This plan touches the runtime pipeline and field.ts lives in the seed; does the ledger of physical words stay here beside the chemistry note, or does it earn a plan of its own once a second quantity is counted?"
}

